# Logs
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# Self-hosted ML weights. Never committed — `scripts/fetch-models.mjs` downloads
# anything pinned in models.lock.json and verifies its sha256.
public/models/

# public/luts/ and public/fonts/ are NOT ignored: the 24 look strips and the 14
# woff2 files are committed so `npm run dev` works on a fresh clone and so the
# test that decodes them can verify the strip layout against LUT3D_FRAG. They are
# generated (`npm run luts:gen`) and repaired (`npm run models:fetch`), not
# hand-edited, and `npm run build` fails if either drifts.

# Playwright (D9-F01). `test-results/` holds traces, screenshots and the
# shader-parity diff image; `playwright-report/` is the generated HTML report.
# Both are per-run, and both are large enough to dominate a diff.
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
.playwright-mcp/
.playwright/

# Visual-audit screenshots. `shots/` is scratch from a whole-product audit — a
# few dozen full-viewport PNGs, regenerable by opening the app again, and not
# referenced by anything. Ignored rather than deleted because the next audit
# writes another one, and AGENTS.md invariant 10 is about directories that exist
# on disk while nothing tracks them: the day somebody wants to commit 24 MB of
# screenshots by accident, `.gitignore` is the place that has already said no.
# A screenshot that *is* a test artefact belongs in `test-results/`, which
# Playwright owns and `npm run test:e2e` wipes for itself.
shots/
